ios: overhead text of stacked players stays on top

Only the first entity standing on a tile's centre is drawn each scene cycle (upstream's tileLastOccupiedCycle); the
others are skipped, so their model is never built and their height (set from the model's top in getTempModel) stays
0, or whatever it was when last drawn. Their chat, health bar, hitsplats and head icons were then placed on the
ground. With hundreds of bots standing on the same tiles at the bank and the hotspots this was common. A skipped
player or NPC now takes the height of the entity drawn on its tile (tileOccupant), so its overhead text sits on top
of the model that is shown there.

diff --git a/src/client/Client.ts b/src/client/Client.ts
index 521d6ee..8f31463 100644
--- a/src/client/Client.ts
+++ b/src/client/Client.ts
